-- ============================================================================
-- T4 - Online Safety Act 2023: links with the United Kingdom
-- Instrument : Online Safety Act 2023 (c. 50)
-- Pinpoint   : s.4(5) and s.4(6)
-- Version    : latest available on legislation.gov.uk - NOT CHECKED. legislation.gov.uk
--              was blocked from the spike environment, so the text below is quoted
--              from the author's knowledge and must be verified before reliance.
-- Evaluated  : 2026-09-23
-- Operative text (UNVERIFIED):
--   (5) For the purposes of subsection (2), a user-to-user service or a search
--       service "has links with the United Kingdom" if -
--       (a) the service has a significant number of United Kingdom users, or
--       (b) United Kingdom users form one of the target markets for the service
--           (or the only target market).
--   (6) A user-to-user service or a search service also "has links with the
--       United Kingdom" if -
--       (a) the service is capable of being used in the United Kingdom by
--           individuals, and
--       (b) there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is a material risk
--           of significant harm to individuals in the United Kingdom presented by -
--           (i) in the case of a user-to-user service, user-generated content
--               present on the service, ...
-- Judgement inputs: "significant number", "target market" and "material risk of
-- significant harm" are human judgements (yes / no / undetermined), never derived.
-- ============================================================================

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT kleene

§ `Online Safety Act 2023 s.4(5)-(6) - links with the United Kingdom`
@ref-map osa-s4 https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2023/50/section/4

DECLARE `UK links limb` IS ONE OF
    `s.4(5)(a) significant number of UK users`
    `s.4(5)(b) UK is a target market`
    `s.4(6) capable of use in the UK and material risk of significant harm`

@ref osa-s4 s.4(5)(a)
GIVEN `significant number of UK users` IS A Judgement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`limb 5(a)` MEANS `the answer to` `significant number of UK users`

@ref osa-s4 s.4(5)(b)
GIVEN `UK is a target market` IS A Judgement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`limb 5(b)` MEANS `the answer to` `UK is a target market`

@ref osa-s4 s.4(6)
GIVEN `capable of use in the UK`         IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `material risk of significant harm` IS A Judgement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`limb 6` MEANS
    `all of` (LIST `capable of use in the UK`,
                   `the answer to` `material risk of significant harm`)

@export The service has links with the United Kingdom (OSA 2023 s.4(5)-(6)). Returns yes, no or undetermined (null).
@ref osa-s4 s.4(5)-(6)
GIVEN `significant number of UK users`    IS A Judgement      @desc s.4(5)(a) judgement
      `UK is a target market`             IS A Judgement      @desc s.4(5)(b) judgement
      `capable of use in the UK`          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc s.4(6)(a) fact; null if unknown
      `material risk of significant harm` IS A Judgement      @desc s.4(6)(b) judgement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`has links with the UK` MEANS
    `any of` (LIST `limb 5(a)` `significant number of UK users`,
                   `limb 5(b)` `UK is a target market`,
                   `limb 6` `capable of use in the UK` `material risk of significant harm`)

-- Which limbs are satisfied (for the explanation).
GIVEN x    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      limb IS A `UK links limb`
GIVETH A LIST OF `UK links limb`
`listed if yes` x limb MEANS
    IF x EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN LIST limb ELSE EMPTY

@export Which s.4(5)-(6) limbs are satisfied. Undetermined limbs are not listed.
GIVEN `significant number of UK users`    IS A Judgement      @desc s.4(5)(a) judgement
      `UK is a target market`             IS A Judgement      @desc s.4(5)(b) judgement
      `capable of use in the UK`          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc s.4(6)(a) fact; null if unknown
      `material risk of significant harm` IS A Judgement      @desc s.4(6)(b) judgement
GIVETH A LIST OF `UK links limb`
`satisfied limbs` MEANS
    concat (LIST `listed if yes` (`limb 5(a)` `significant number of UK users`)
                                 `s.4(5)(a) significant number of UK users`,
                 `listed if yes` (`limb 5(b)` `UK is a target market`)
                                 `s.4(5)(b) UK is a target market`,
                 `listed if yes` (`limb 6` `capable of use in the UK` `material risk of significant harm`)
                                 `s.4(6) capable of use in the UK and material risk of significant harm`)
